raph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAsyncBatcher"},{"type":"text","value":" hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PreactAsyncBatcherOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreactAsyncBatcherOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", {\n}>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"item"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Batch API requests\nconst batchApiCall = useAsyncBatchedCallback(async (requests: ApiRequest[]) => {\n  const results = await Promise.all(requests.map(req => fetch(req.url)));\n  return results.map(res => res.json());\n}, {\n  maxSize: 10,   // Process when 10 requests collected\n  wait: 1000     // Or after 1 second\n});\n\n// Use in event handlers\n<button onClick={() => batchApiCall({ url: '/api/analytics', data: eventData })}>\n  Track Event\n</button>","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncBatchedCallback<TValue>(fn, options): (item) => Promise<void>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-batcher/useAsyncBatchedCallback.ts:42](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/async-batcher/useAsyncBatchedCallback.ts#L42)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a batched version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the `useAsyncBatcher` hook,\nproviding a stable, batched async function reference for use in Preact components.\n\nThe batched async function will collect individual calls into batches and execute them\nwhen batch conditions are met (max size reached, wait time elapsed, or custom logic).\nThe returned function always returns a promise that resolves with undefined (since the\nbatch function processes multiple items together).\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useAsyncBatcher`, making it ideal for basic\nasync batching needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncBatcher instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual batch execution\n- Access to batch results and state\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useAsyncBatcher` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `Promise`\\<`unknown`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactAsyncBatcherOptions`](../interfaces/PreactAsyncBatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(`item`) => `Promise`\\<`void`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Batch API requests\nconst batchApiCall = useAsyncBatchedCallback(async (requests: ApiRequest[]) => {\n  const results = await Promise.all(requests.map(req => fetch(req.url)));\n  return results.map(res => res.json());\n}, {\n  maxSize: 10,   // Process when 10 requests collected\n  wait: 1000     // Or after 1 second\n});\n\n// Use in event handlers\n<button onClick={() => batchApiCall({ url: '/api/analytics', data: eventData })}>\n  Track Event\n</button>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useAsyncBatchedCallback\ntitle: useAsyncBatchedCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncBatchedCallback<TValue>(fn, options): (item) => Promise<void>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-batcher/useAsyncBatchedCallback.ts:42](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/async-batcher/useAsyncBatchedCallback.ts#L42)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a batched version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the `useAsyncBatcher` hook,\nproviding a stable, batched async function reference for use in Preact components.\n\nThe batched async function will collect individual calls into batches and execute them\nwhen batch conditions are met (max size reached, wait time elapsed, or custom logic).\nThe returned function always returns a promise that resolves with undefined (since the\nbatch function processes multiple items together).\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useAsyncBatcher`, making it ideal for basic\nasync batching needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncBatcher instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual batch execution\n- Access to batch results and state\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useAsyncBatcher` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `Promise`\\<`unknown`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactAsyncBatcherOptions`](../interfaces/PreactAsyncBatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(`item`) => `Promise`\\<`void`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Batch API requests\nconst batchApiCall = useAsyncBatchedCallback(async (requests: ApiRequest[]) => {\n  const results = await Promise.all(requests.map(req => fetch(req.url)));\n  return results.map(res => res.json());\n}, {\n  maxSize: 10,   // Process when 10 requests collected\n  wait: 1000     // Or after 1 second\n});\n\n// Use in event handlers\n<button onClick={() => batchApiCall({ url: '/api/analytics', data: eventData })}>\n  Track Event\n</button>\n```\n"}
